        "responses": {
          "values": [
            {
              "role": "system",
              "content": "=Classify this email reply into exactly one category.\n\nCategories:\nPAYMENT_PROMISE - commits to a payment date, explicit or implied (\"will send Friday\")\nALREADY_PAID - claims payment was already sent\nDISPUTE - disputes the amount, the invoice itself, or work delivered\nNEGOTIATION - asks for a payment plan, extension, or partial payment\nQUESTION - asks something but doesn't commit either way\nSTOP - asks not to be contacted, or uses legal/harassment language\nAUTO_REPLY - out of office, bounce, autoresponder\n\nIf the category is PAYMENT_PROMISE, also extract the exact phrase used for timing (e.g. \"Friday\", \"next Monday\", \"in 3 days\", \"end of month\") as promised_date_phrase. Do not calculate an actual calendar date yourself — just return the phrase as written.\n\nReturn ONLY valid JSON, no markdown fences:\n{\"category\":\"...\", \"confidence\":0.0-1.0, \"promised_date_phrase\":\"... or null\", \"summary\":\"under 15 words\"}"
            },
            {
              "content": "={{ $json.reply }}"
            }
          ]
        },
        "builtInTools": {},
        "options": {
          "temperature": 0
        }
      },
      "type": "@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.openAi",
      "typeVersion": 2.3,
      "position": [
        2704,
        -352
      ],
      "id": "03f29478-94a4-4de7-8009-ba841b5e7c1e",
      "name": "Classify Reply",
      "credentials": {
        "openAiApi": {
          "id": "QKspIILvOeEnfNO4",
          "name": "OpenAI account"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "jsCode": "const classification = (() => {\n  const raw = $json.output?.[0]?.content?.[0]?.text ?? $json.message?.content ?? $json.content ?? \"{}\";\n  try {\n    return typeof raw === \"string\" ? JSON.parse(raw.replace(/```json|```/g, \"\").trim()) : raw;\n  } catch (e) {\n    return { category: \"QUESTION\", confidence: 0, summary: \"unparseable\" };\n  }\n})();\n\nconst replyText = $('Extract Reply Text').item.json.reply || \"\";\n\nconst weekdays = [\"sunday\",\"monday\",\"tuesday\",\"wednesday\",\"thursday\",\"friday\",\"saturday\"];\n\nfunction nextWeekday(name) {\n  const target = weekdays.indexOf(name.toLowerCase());\n  if (target === -1) return null;\n  const today = new Date();\n  const todayDow = today.getDay();\n  let diff = (target - todayDow + 7) % 7;\n  if (diff === 0) diff = 7; // \"Friday\" said on a Friday means next Friday, not today\n  const result = new Date(today);\n  result.setDate(today.getDate() + diff);\n  return result.toISOString().slice(0, 10);\n}\n\nlet promisedDate = null;\nconst dayMatch = replyText.match(/\\b(sunday|monday|tuesday|wednesday|thursday|friday|saturday)\\b/i);\nconst tomorrowMatch = /\\btomorrow\\b/i.test(replyText);\nconst todayMatch = /\\btoday\\b/i.test(replyText);\n\nif (todayMatch) {\n  promisedDate = new Date().toISOString().slice(0, 10);\n} else if (tomorrowMatch) {\n  const d = new Date();\n  d.setDate(d.getDate() + 1);\n  promisedDate = d.toISOString().slice(0, 10);\n} else if (dayMatch) {\n  promisedDate = nextWeekday(dayMatch[1]);\n}\n\nreturn [{ json: {\n  ...$('Extract Reply Text').item.json,\n  category: classification.category,\n  confidence: classification.confidence,\n  summary: classification.summary,\n  promised_date: promisedDate\n} }];"
      },
